[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:Do the English Speak English?]
[00:16.35]Why does the writer not understand the porter?
[00:23.44]I arrived in London at last.
[00:27.19]The railway station was big, black and dark.
[00:33.39]I did not know the way to my hotel, so I asked a porter.
[00:39.75]I not only spoke English very carefully, but very clearly as well.
[00:47.61]The porter, however, could not understand me.
[00:52.48]I repeated my question several times and at last he understood.
[01:00.39]he answered me, but he spoke neither slowly nor clearly.
[01:07.77]'I am a foreigner,' I said.
[01:11.76]Then he spoke slowly,
[01:14.72]but I could not understand him.
[01:17.88]My teacher never spoke English like that!
[01:22.45]The porter and I looked at each other and smiled.
[01:28.15]Then he said something and I understood it.
[01:32.75]'You'll soon learn English!' he said.
[01:37.94]I wonder.
[01:39.93]In England, each person speaks a different language.
[01:44.67]The English understand each other, but I don't understand them!
[01:50.19]Do they speak English?
